WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:09.740
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:20.270
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.460
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:06.940
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:14.210
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:20.950
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:28.380
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.630
Rimone…

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.010
Rimone, the elder is summoning you.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.020
Aira and Hanna are going
to give it a try today!

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.750
Ah, here she is now.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.000
Rimone!

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.340
Aira, Hanna…

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.020
Are you really sure you want to do this?

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:40.430
Of course!

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:43.500
You know how long we’ve been
practicing towards this day!

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.970
I’m so glad they chose me!

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:50.270
It’s always been my dream to
be like you and Dominüra…

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.770
…and to do the Emerald Ri Majon!

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.690
Sibylla Dominüra and Sibylla Rimone…

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:03.400
It was they who bestowed us
with the Emerald Ri Majon.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.490
And now our young girls
have taken to the skies.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.360
We have seen flowers blooming
that had never bloomed before…

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.750
…and we are now reaping the
harvest of our barren crops.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.010
And now today, we shall
send off two more girls.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:22.760
I am certain that they, too,
shall bring us great fortune!

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:51.290
<b>Their Portraits</b>

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:04.390
Get a move on! Let’s not keep
the client waiting forever!

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.390
Morinas…

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.470
Well, what is it, Wauf?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.290
Listen to me.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.560
It doesn’t matter if
you’re a man or a woman…

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.690
…or even a former sibylla,
for that matter.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:20.670
You work for me now! And I’m
not cutting you any slack.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.860
Right, right, so what’s up?

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.860
Are you telling me to pick up the pace?

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.200
You need to go easy on yourself.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.080
Daddy!

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.230
Hey, what is it, sweetheart?

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.180
Mommy said…

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.710
…to ask you what you wanted for lunch.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:39.250
Well, everything your
mommy makes is so delicious.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.630
She said you’re not
allowed to say “anything”!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.470
She did? All right, that’s
going to be a tough one then.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.470
So listen, this is the
most critical time for you!

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:55.810
I don’t want Waporif coming
after me if you overdo it.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:05:00.140
I’ve heard that if you just keep moving,
you can pop out the baby, 1-2-3!

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:01.570
Is that right?

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:04.350
But thanks.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:07.410
So what are we having for lunch, Daddy?

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.780
Hm, let’s see now…

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.520
Morinas!

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:14.960
Hey, good work.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.330
Hold on a second, didn’t you
just finish your night shift?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.790
Well, we don’t have a choice.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.760
The highlands and Shoukoku
are already waging a cold war.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:27.750
They could void the peace treaty any
day, and then they’ll drag us into it!

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.550
War again, huh?

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:32.010
Eliph! Let’s go!

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:32.810
Okay!

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.310
See you!

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.710
They saved us back there, didn’t they?

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:02.880
Yes, they did.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:04.960
Floe was crying.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:06.720
I know.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.220
Do you think we’ll succeed?

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.350
The Emerald Ri Majon?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:13.900
Yes.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:30.320
You’ve stolen a Simoun and
allowed the sibyllae to escape.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.990
Do you realize the magnitude
of what you’ve done?

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:39.710
If they should revolt
against our country…

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:42.290
You’ve got the wrong idea.
All they’re going to do…

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.670
…is carry themselves away.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.630
To the Land of Hope.

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:04.770
Paraietta!

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:05.940
Play with us!

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.950
I have a guest to tend to now, so
it’ll have to be a little later.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.490
Everyone, try to get along now!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.450
Yes, ma’am!

00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:18.910
Such lively children!

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.460
I know. It’s all I can
do to keep up with them.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.000
Paraietta, I’m so sorry.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.880
I tried to negotiate with them, but…

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.320
…there’s not much more I can do.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.470
Roatreamon…

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.430
…this place wouldn’t even
exist without your help.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.430
And I’m so grateful for that.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:37.960
Well, there has to be
another way. I’ll find one.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.350
Once war is officially declared…

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:44.320
…there will be more and more
victims like these children.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.440
They’re not really victims though.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:51.370
Right. They’ve lost a
lot because of the war…

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:54.950
…but they still have
so much to live for!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.030
They’re our seeds of hope.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:01.580
Their footsteps will one day
ring out across the Land of Hope.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:03.940
Of Hope…

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:13.130
“The Land of Hope.”

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:16.970
For someone who was once
a priestess long ago…

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:19.810
…those words have
such a nostalgic ring.

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:22.690
I thought it was only a legend.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:29.830
But even if the legend is true…

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:36.200
…what purpose could there be in
performing the Emerald Ri Majon now?

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:40.740
There’s no longer any
value to the word “purpose.”

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:41.790
Anubituf…

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:47.130
Yes, if we looked hard enough,
we might find such a purpose.

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:49.850
But even if we’d found one…

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:53.120
…the girls would never
have chosen it themselves.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:58.800
What?

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.510
The Simouns…

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:06.650
Take our Simouns and pursue
the Sibylla Aurea’s Simoun!

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:09.520
Are you insane? Do you
intend to shoot them down?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:35.880
Chief!

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.970
Our hands are tied. There’s
nothing we can do now.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.350
We’re going to go back to our jobs now!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.100
Yes, sir!

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.860
It will be all right, Floe.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.190
They’ll be fine.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.020
Even if they go after them now…

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:58.860
But, but…

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:02.890
I’m sure that Aer and
Neviril will make it in time.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.580
It’s going to be all right.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:07.190
Here, your nose is running!

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:12.590
Really, since when are
you such a crybaby, Floe?

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.460
But, but…

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.720
Floe, there’s no need to worry.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:18.840
Don’t cry.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:22.720
Yeah, come on. I’m
sure Aer and Neviril…

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:23.960
Huh? What?

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:25.220
Para-sama, you’re breathing on me…

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:26.570
What? Oh no!

00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:29.060
Okay! I’m gonna get
all touchy-feely too!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.360
Oh? Then let’s do that too!

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:33.030
— Para-sama!
— Me too!

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:35.480
Come on! Stop it, Alty!

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:56.090
Big Sister, was that…

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.090
Yes.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.850
Big Sister! Hurry, hurry!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.680
Dad’s clothes! Alty! Get that one!

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:12.110
Oh, brother. All that time
we spent doing laundry…

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:15.190
This weather’s so weird. Guess we’ll
just have to wash everything again.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.980
Hey, all you do is sit
there and watch, Big Sister!

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:20.090
Well, that’s my job.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.630
Dummy!

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:50.980
Dominüra…

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.590
Are you feeling any better?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.450
Thank you. My fever has gone down.

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:19.760
That’s good.

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:21.920
Is something the matter?

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:24.030
I think I finally understand…

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:27.200
…what you meant after all this time.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.720
They’re all going to fly off.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:33.730
Into a sky where nothing
is ever certain…

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:37.730
Towards a hope that they
can’t even be sure exists.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:41.530
I made everyone learn how
to do the Emerald Ri Majon…

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.900
…yet I don’t even
take to the skies myself.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:45.660
I…

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.260
Rimone…

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.500
Do you want to fly again?

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:52.370
Yes.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:55.430
But if you don’t want
to do it, Dominüra…

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.740
I’ll never fly with anyone as my pair…

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:01.370
…but you, Dominüra.

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:15.730
I’m going to do it for you.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.570
The Emerald Ri Majon.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:25.070
Simouns!

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:26.820
They’re coming after us!

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.070
— Neviril!
— Yes.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.980
Let’s hurry! They’re
going to catch up to us.

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:32.580
— Wait.
— What?

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.420
They’re going to do a Ri Majon!

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.670
We’d better hurry up then!

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:41.290
No. That’s…

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:44.300
What is it?

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:46.550
I’ve never seen that Ri Majon before.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.800
The Morning Calm Ri Majon.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:51.050
Morning Calm?

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.350
I read about that one
once in an old book.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.850
It’s performed to bid farewell to
comrades about to depart on a journey.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:01.110
To bid farewell to comrades
departing on a journey…

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.370
But that’s…

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.830
The Morning Calm Ri Majon?

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:25.840
There was also a time in my life…

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:31.140
Long ago, we were all maidens too.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.120
Let’s do it.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.160
Yes.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:58.080
Let’s do it now.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.260
Let’s go now, Aer…

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:12.010
To a place where you and I can be free!

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:15.740
Yes. Let’s go, Neviril!

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:27.130
Forgive me for bringing
you here, Rimone.

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.860
That’s all right. What is it?

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:33.070
You see, I want you to pair up with me.

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:37.160
I already told you no once.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.540
I’ll only…

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.080
I know that.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:46.430
But does Dominüra ever intend
to fly again? I wonder…

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.550
I’m sorry.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:54.300
Still…

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:13.820
Um, wasn’t that a Simoun?

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.620
Aer!

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.780
Huh? What’s that?

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.290
Is that a name?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.170
The ultimate form of love.

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:25.380
Love?

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.750
That’s right.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.250
Dominüra!

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:32.320
The ultimate love.

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:35.470
Which sky shall we journey towards next?

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.470
Dominüra!

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:11.250
Hey! You got here early, Vura!

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:13.510
No, wait. I mean Vuraf.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.260
It’s awkward for you
to call me that, right?

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:16.510
You can just call me Vura.

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:19.470
All right, Vura. Why
don’t you come inside?

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.510
Sure.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:27.150
Did you get one too, Vura?

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.020
Yeah.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.520
The war hasn’t even started yet!

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:33.230
I guess former sibyllae…

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:36.530
…have the honor of being the first
to be shipped out at times like these.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.070
Which side?

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:41.450
My hometown is on the
other side of the border.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:43.090
I’ll be fighting for Shoukoku.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.660
So we’re going to be enemies then?

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:46.540
Yeah.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:52.700
Never mind. Here, have some of our
local vegetables! New strain, you know.

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:54.630
I need to make a killing on these…

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:58.380
…and find myself a lovely bride.
I can’t die till I’ve done that!

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:02.680
Becoming a man hasn’t
changed you at all, Floef!

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.020
It’s hard to say, isn’t it?
You can just call me Floe too.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.860
Is that the Arcus Prima?

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:21.530
Yeah. I thought I might as well
live where I can always see it.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.030
That’s why I picked this spot.

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:25.160
A sunken luxury liner?

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:27.860
I suppose there’s an allure to that.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:29.920
See you then.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.040
Yeah, see you later.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:33.550
Wait, that might be bad luck to say.

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:36.210
I don’t want to see
you on the battlefield.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:39.090
All right then. How’s goodbye?

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:41.890
Right. Goodbye.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:42.940
Bye.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:09.840
I wonder why none of us could let it go?

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:14.090
The idea of sending Aer and
Neviril off to that other world?

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:20.090
Was it because we wanted to defy
the inescapable flow of time?

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:23.010
We were afraid to grow up.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:25.100
We wanted to stay the way
we were as young girls.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:28.590
Did we project those feelings
on to Aer and Neviril?

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.600
No, I’m sure that’s not it.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:35.110
All we wanted to do
was to leave our mark.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:39.610
To prove that we once
existed, right here.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:42.110
We wanted to shout that
out to the whole world.

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:47.410
The fact that we were
once really here…

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.280
We wanted to leave our mark.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:53.080
We wanted to raise our voices.

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:03.590
Aer…

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:04.960
Neviril…

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:09.140
I wonder where you are right now?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:17.020
Where are you, our eternal maidens?

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.580
Such a nice breeze.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.040
Yes.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.920
It certainly is a nice breeze.

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:47.900
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:52.140
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:59.210
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.210 --> 00:23:06.810
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.620 --> 00:23:19.700
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:24.870
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:28.850
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:32.880
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:38.750
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:44.300
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.300 --> 00:23:47.730
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:53.400
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:59.630
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>
